{"content":[{"c":["RACHEL’S TOMB"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Landmark set up by Jacob at the site of Rachel’s grave (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.35.19-20","r":"Gen.35.19-20","rawR":"Gen.35.19-20","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.35.19-20","value":"Gen.35.19-20"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 35:19-20"},") that was still in existence at the time of Samuel (",{"href":"?bref=1Sam.10.2","r":"1Sam.10.2","rawR":"1Sam.10.2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Sam.10.2","value":"1Sam.10.2"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Sm 10:2"},"). Two persisting traditions make its original location still questionable. The older tradition locates the tomb near Bethlehem, south of Jerusalem (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.35.19","r":"Gen.35.19","rawR":"Gen.35.19","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.35.19","value":"Gen.35.19"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 35:19"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Gen.48.7","r":"Gen.48.7","rawR":"Gen.48.7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.48.7","value":"Gen.48.7"}],"t":"ref","v":"48:7"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Matt.2.18","r":"Matt.2.18","rawR":"Matt.2.18","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Matt.2.18","value":"Matt.2.18"}],"t":"ref","v":"Mt 2:18"},"). This option has won the impressive historical support of Josephus, Eusebius, Jerome, Origen, and the Talmudists. A second site is Ephrath (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.35.19","r":"Gen.35.19","rawR":"Gen.35.19","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.35.19","value":"Gen.35.19"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 35:19"},"), which was on the northern border of Benjamin, 10 miles (16.1 kilometers) north of Jerusalem (",{"href":"?bref=1Sam.10.2","r":"1Sam.10.2","rawR":"1Sam.10.2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Sam.10.2","value":"1Sam.10.2"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Sm 10:2"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Jer.31.15","r":"Jer.31.15","rawR":"Jer.31.15","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Jer.31.15","value":"Jer.31.15"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jer 31:15"},"), near ancient Bethel."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"},{"c":["Rachel’s tomb is the first recorded instance in the Bible of a sepulchral monument. A picture of the tomb is a common decorative piece in Jewish homes throughout the world."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"RachelsTomb","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Gn 35:19-20","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.35.19-20","rawQueryValue":"Gen.35.19-20","sourceRefExact":"Gen.35.19-20"},{"anchorText":"1 Sm 10:2","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Sam.10.2","rawQueryValue":"1Sam.10.2","sourceRefExact":"1Sam.10.2"},{"anchorText":"Gn 35:19","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.35.19","rawQueryValue":"Gen.35.19","sourceRefExact":"Gen.35.19"},{"anchorText":"48:7","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.48.7","rawQueryValue":"Gen.48.7","sourceRefExact":"Gen.48.7"},{"anchorText":"Mt 2:18","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Matt.2.18","rawQueryValue":"Matt.2.18","sourceRefExact":"Matt.2.18"},{"anchorText":"Gn 35:19","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.35.19","rawQueryValue":"Gen.35.19","sourceRefExact":"Gen.35.19"},{"anchorText":"1 Sm 10:2","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Sam.10.2","rawQueryValue":"1Sam.10.2","sourceRefExact":"1Sam.10.2"},{"anchorText":"Jer 31:15","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Jer.31.15","rawQueryValue":"Jer.31.15","sourceRefExact":"Jer.31.15"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"a99ef18001cec096103376bdd7dbab6f2c4822b9c4ddd721b8f4f5c2f3c5e034","sourceItemName":"RachelsTomb","sourceItemOrder":17,"sourceMember":"Articles/R.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"RachelsTomb","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Rachel’s Tomb","title":"Rachel’s Tomb","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}